      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## When to use\nUse when building, reimplementing, or fixing a Powerhouse document editor or drive app \u2014 the React UI that displays and edits documents of a given model in Connect.\n\n## What it covers\n- Workflow\n- Common mistakes\n- ED.00.1 Familiarize yourself with the document model\n- ED.00.2 Scaffold the editor via the CLI (primary route)\n- ED.00.3 Alternative: register through the Vetra Drive\n- ED.00.4 Verify the code generation was triggered and boilerplate code was created\n- ED.01.1 Verify code generation and clean up the boilerplate code\n- ED.01.2 Ensure test documents exist for verification\n- ED.01.3 Implement viewing functionality\n- ED.01.4 Implement editing functionality\n- ED.01.5 Resolve outstanding issues\n- ED.01.6 Visual verification with Playwright\n- Required imports and setup\n- Styling\n\n## Where the full skill lives\n- Vault source: **Agent skill: document-editor** (full text, DERIVED_FROM below) \u2014 the vault is this skill's home.\n- Upstream origin: https://github.com/powerhouse-inc/powerhouse-dev-skills/tree/main/skills/document-editor\n\n## Invocation\nRead the vault source content and follow it. Not a plugin command.\n\n_Added via add-skill; content hash sha256:54c107cb7ab1\u2026_",
